    "temple_short_bio": "The 15th Shiva temple on the northern bank of the Cauvery River celebrated in the Tevaram hymns by the Saivite saints. The temple is deeply celebrated for a divine miracle involving the child-saint Thirugnana Sambandar, who was gifted a pair of golden cymbals (thalam) by Lord Shiva to accompany his devotional singing, while Goddess Parvati infused them with sound."
